      "textEn": "\nHey! Danu bore eighty-one sons, eighteen of which were prominent. Their names are as follows—\nDvimurdha, Shambara, Arishta, Hayagriva, Vibhavasu, Ayomukha, Shankushira, Swarabhanu, Kapila, Aruna,\nPuloma, Vrishaparva, Ekachakra, Anutapana, Dhumrakesh, Virupaksha, Viprachiti, and Durjaya. Swarbhano Suprabhaan Kanyamuhaah Namuchiha. Vrushaparvanastu sharmishtam yayatirnahusho bali. 32. Meaning of the word\n\nSwarbhanoah - of Swarbhanu; Suprabham - bright; Kanyam - maiden, daughter; Uvah - married; Namuchih - Namuchi's; Kil-\nUndoubtedly; Vrishaparvanah - of Vrishaparva; Tu - but; Sharmishtam - Sharmishta; Yayatih - King Yayati; Nahushah - son of Nahusha;\nBali - extremely strong. Namuchi married Suprabha, the daughter of Swarbhanu. Sharmistha, the daughter of Vrishaparva, was given to Nahusha's\nson, the mighty king Yayati. Vaishvanarasuta yaschatasracharudarshanah. Upadanvi Hayashira Puloma Kalka and others. 33. Upadanvi Hiranyakshah Kraturhayasiram Nrip.\nPuloman Kalka cha dwa vaishvanarasute tu kah. 34). Upayematha Bhagavan Kashyapo Brahmachoditah."
